(2654453, 366213, 30049, '<td valign="top">This is nice.  Too bad you couldn''t have caught this same scene with just a little dew on the spider web to bring it out more.  Nonetheless, it''s a good fine and photographed well overall.  It has a sense of darkness and is a little surreal with the foggy/blurred background.</td>', 'This is nice.  Too bad you couldn''t have caught this same scene with just a little dew on the spider web to bring it out more.  Nonetheless, it''s a good fine and photographed well overall.  It has a sense of darkness and is a little surreal with the foggy/blurred background.', '2006-07-24 10:40:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(2654468, 364908, 30049, '<td valign="top">This is a cool shot.  Nice texture and tones.  Did you consider cropping top and right out some, leaving just the left steps, the round circle, and most of the inside rounded wall?  I ask because the area behind the wrought-iron fence is distracting.  I imagine you wanted to include the fence because it has lines as well, but the composition could have been stronger without it. It would have also moved the flower circle off-center some. JMO of course.  ;^)</td>', 'This is a cool shot.  Nice texture and tones.  Did you consider cropping top and right out some, leaving just the left steps, the round circle, and most of the inside rounded wall?  I ask because the area behind the wrought-iron fence is distracting.  I imagine you wanted to include the fence because it has lines as well, but the composition could have been stronger without it. It would have also moved the flower circle off-center some. JMO of course.  ;^)', '2006-07-24 10:45:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(2654472, 365321, 30049, '<td valign="top">Nice catch.  I love seeing the light coming thru the trees and fog (or smoke).  Good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'Nice catch.  I love seeing the light coming thru the trees and fog (or smoke).  Good luck in the challenge.', '2006-07-24 10:46:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(2654484, 364610, 30049, '<td valign="top">Now I''m going to have to look for this!  ;^)  Unless, of course, you mean Fredericksburg, Texas...I''m assuming Virginia.  Good luck neighbor!<br/> <br/>Concerning the image, there are certainly lines to use.  Did you consider closing the right door enough to block that back window (given permission to do do)?  I think that window is distracting a little.  Doors closed maybe?  A touch more contrast could liven up the exterior wall some.  Just some thoughts, and all JMO.</td>', 'Now I''m going to have to look for this!  ;^)  Unless, of course, you mean Fredericksburg, Texas...I''m assuming Virginia.  Good luck neighbor! Concerning the image, there are certainly lines to use.  Did you consider closing the right door enough to block that back window (given permission to do do)?  I think that window is distracting a little.  Doors closed maybe?  A touch more contrast could liven up the exterior wall some.  Just some thoughts, and all JMO.', '2006-07-24 10:49:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(2654488, 366082, 30049, '<td valign="top">Yep.  Ribbon material here for sure!  Clean, simple, good use of DOF to add another dimension to the image.  The green color pop really jumps out.  Congrats in advance.  ;^)</td>', 'Yep.  Ribbon material here for sure!  Clean, simple, good use of DOF to add another dimension to the image.  The green color pop really jumps out.  Congrats in advance.  ;^)', '2006-07-24 10:51:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(2654521, 362709, 30049, '<td valign="top">Most of the time I see guitar shots going the opposite direction, down the neck.  Your approach is fresh.  The DOF is hurting this a little, as it''s hard to see much in focus.  I''m not saying that some of it isn''t in focus, just a large portion is not.  Guessing by the light and reflections, you were near a window for light?  Seems a bit strong on the left side of your photo.  Did you consider trimming about 1/3 off the left side of this?  Would have given more impact to the lines portion of this.  All of this is obviously, JMO.  ;^)  Good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'Most of the time I see guitar shots going the opposite direction, down the neck.  Your approach is fresh.  The DOF is hurting this a little, as it''s hard to see much in focus.  I''m not saying that some of it isn''t in focus, just a large portion is not.  Guessing by the light and reflections, you were near a window for light?  Seems a bit strong on the left side of your photo.  Did you consider trimming about 1/3 off the left side of this?  Would have given more impact to the lines portion of this.  All of this is obviously, JMO.  ;^)  Good luck in the challenge.', '2006-07-24 11:12:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(2654822, 365620, 56400, '<td valign="top">Love the color and texture.</td>', 'Love the color and texture.', '2006-07-24 12:49:24.000000', NULL, 1),
