(2667479, 364948, 39664, '<td valign="top">Here is a little bit of unsolicited advice from one who has been at the bottom here more than once.....Powerlines are the biggest pain in the butt for all photographers.....they are considered a distraction in a photograph and if you only have basic editing, you can''t take them out!  So, by knowing they are the bane of all photographer''s existance, a shot of just the powerlines just doesn''t appeal to the majority, especially on a site like this where the folks are ultra-critical.  <br/> <br/>Just my 2 cents, for what it''s worth and I''m just trying to help.  :-)</td>', 'Here is a little bit of unsolicited advice from one who has been at the bottom here more than once.....Powerlines are the biggest pain in the butt for all photographers.....they are considered a distraction in a photograph and if you only have basic editing, you can''t take them out!  So, by knowing they are the bane of all photographer''s existance, a shot of just the powerlines just doesn''t appeal to the majority, especially on a site like this where the folks are ultra-critical.   Just my 2 cents, for what it''s worth and I''m just trying to help.  :-)', '2006-07-27 12:09:26.000000', NULL, 0),
