(2669221, 365525, 11793, '<td valign="top">i had this one picked for top ten at least.  nice work and congrats !<br/> <br/>your finishing score is about where mine started - errr ;}<br/> <br/></td>', 'i had this one picked for top ten at least.  nice work and congrats ! your finishing score is about where mine started - errr ;} ', '2006-07-27 19:58:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(2669255, 364840, 22301, '<td valign="top">Konador, Thanks for my comment on my beach entry and I only wish you were right! I have decided to give a comment on all commentors on my shot. I am think this was a good shot for the lines challenge, some suggestions that I could make would maybe be a different crop where more of the reflections of the building were present so that the eye could follow it to the building. the water looks really smooth and its almost hard to tell if the building pilings go deep in the ground or if the water is just an inch or two high. good placement to considering the size of the pchallenge. thanks again for your comment.</td>', 'Konador, Thanks for my comment on my beach entry and I only wish you were right! I have decided to give a comment on all commentors on my shot. I am think this was a good shot for the lines challenge, some suggestions that I could make would maybe be a different crop where more of the reflections of the building were present so that the eye could follow it to the building. the water looks really smooth and its almost hard to tell if the building pilings go deep in the ground or if the water is just an inch or two high. good placement to considering the size of the pchallenge. thanks again for your comment.', '2006-07-27 20:09:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(2669319, 364759, 17851, '<td valign="top">nice macro! The complimentary colors work very well and the focus is good. I would use some noise reduction and saturate the reds of the bug a little more. :)</td>', 'nice macro! The complimentary colors work very well and the focus is good. I would use some noise reduction and saturate the reds of the bug a little more. :)', '2006-07-27 20:31:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(2669386, 362935, 22301, '<td valign="top">Richard, <br/>thanks for your comment on my beach entry and I thought I would return the favor. This is a very cool shot and I like your take on lines and the lighting is great. I agree with one of the commentors that the crop on the thumb is too tight. Since it is the main subject I think it would have helped to have the whole thumb in the frame. I thnk I would have given this a six and if your thumb was all the way in a 7 or 8. Its a good shot but the dynamic lines and strange perspective I think held you back from a better score because that isn''t what most DPC voters like to see. But I like it! Thanks again for your comment.<br/>Joe</td>', 'Richard, thanks for your comment on my beach entry and I thought I would return the favor. This is a very cool shot and I like your take on lines and the lighting is great. I agree with one of the commentors that the crop on the thumb is too tight. Since it is the main subject I think it would have helped to have the whole thumb in the frame. I thnk I would have given this a six and if your thumb was all the way in a 7 or 8. Its a good shot but the dynamic lines and strange perspective I think held you back from a better score because that isn''t what most DPC voters like to see. But I like it! Thanks again for your comment.Joe', '2006-07-27 20:54:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(2669408, 365694, 22301, '<td valign="top">Mark, <br/>Thanks for your comment on my Beach entry, I thoguth I would return the favor. This definitely has lines running through it! I think I would have maybe had the entire image  be alittle brighter, perhaps just a little slower shutter speed, this would have made the lines even brighter. Just a suggestion, thanks again for your comment.<br/>joe</td>', 'Mark, Thanks for your comment on my Beach entry, I thoguth I would return the favor. This definitely has lines running through it! I think I would have maybe had the entire image  be alittle brighter, perhaps just a little slower shutter speed, this would have made the lines even brighter. Just a suggestion, thanks again for your comment.joe', '2006-07-27 20:59:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(2669426, 362906, 22301, '<td valign="top">Router guy, <br/>Thanks for your comment on my Beach entry and thought I would return the favor, and thanks for voting as if it was basic editing even if you weren''t sure. I think this is a great entry and thought that this would have score alittle bit higher. I am not sure how wide you shot this at, but maybe using the widest angle on your lens would have allowed you to get closer to the lines and make them more prevalent. Also it feels like you were just off to the right of center when you took  the photo, maybe taking the photo here would have helped abit also. Thanks for your comment again, and these are just some suggestions.<br/>joe</td>', 'Router guy, Thanks for your comment on my Beach entry and thought I would return the favor, and thanks for voting as if it was basic editing even if you weren''t sure. I think this is a great entry and thought that this would have score alittle bit higher. I am not sure how wide you shot this at, but maybe using the widest angle on your lens would have allowed you to get closer to the lines and make them more prevalent. Also it feels like you were just off to the right of center when you took  the photo, maybe taking the photo here would have helped abit also. Thanks for your comment again, and these are just some suggestions.joe', '2006-07-27 21:06:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(2669443, 363150, 22301, '<td valign="top">Urfa, <br/>Thanks for your coment on my Beach entry and I thought I would return the favor.  I think this has some really strong lines and is a cool find. A suggestion right off the top is to have your photo be a larger file size. The max allowable is 150 kb and your is 58 kb. This means you could have had hearly three times the smoothness in edges and details. I notice this is one ting that can keep a score down abit. Here is a <a href="//dpchallenge.com/tutorial.php?TUTORIAL_ID=26" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">link</a> to he photoshop tutorial on this site for submitting photos for challenges. But I thikn you had a used a good perspective and like the wide angle feel. Thanks again.<br/>joe</td>', 'Urfa, Thanks for your coment on my Beach entry and I thought I would return the favor.  I think this has some really strong lines and is a cool find. A suggestion right off the top is to have your photo be a larger file size. The max allowable is 150 kb and your is 58 kb. This means you could have had hearly three times the smoothness in edges and details. I notice this is one ting that can keep a score down abit. Here is a link to he photoshop tutorial on this site for submitting photos for challenges. But I thikn you had a used a good perspective and like the wide angle feel. Thanks again.joe', '2006-07-27 21:13:28.000000', NULL, 0),
