(2673384, 365989, 57229, '<td valign="top">Just a thought - if you''re hungry for dpc success - a little secondary subject might have helped.<br/> <br/>This is <b>very</b> well put together as it is, with the two set of lines ''lining up'', as it were. It''s balanced and understated, so I can see a good argument for not spoiling that.<br/> <br/>A little hand on the wire? Something ''left''?<br/> <br/>I prefer it without those things, but ??</td>', 'Just a thought - if you''re hungry for dpc success - a little secondary subject might have helped. This is very well put together as it is, with the two set of lines ''lining up'', as it were. It''s balanced and understated, so I can see a good argument for not spoiling that. A little hand on the wire? Something ''left''? I prefer it without those things, but ??', '2006-07-29 05:30:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(2673387, 362794, 22937, '<td valign="top">This shot was made using an external Speedlite incl. transmitter. The lightsource was ponted skywards. On top of it I placed a transparent plastic box (some sort of dvd cover!?) A hazel leaf (Hasselblad in Swedish) was then placed inside the box right above the flash - you can see this leaf in the background as diffuse large lines. Then I placed the second leaf on top of the box appr. 1" above the first leaf. That pretty much sums it all up.<br/> <br/>/Fredrik<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-07-29 04:51:44.</i></td>', 'This shot was made using an external Speedlite incl. transmitter. The lightsource was ponted skywards. On top of it I placed a transparent plastic box (some sort of dvd cover!?) A hazel leaf (Hasselblad in Swedish) was then placed inside the box right above the flash - you can see this leaf in the background as diffuse large lines. Then I placed the second leaf on top of the box appr. 1" above the first leaf. That pretty much sums it all up. /Fredrik', '2006-07-29 05:37:25.000000', '2006-07-29 05:51:44.000000', 0),
(2673522, 364108, 7889, '<td valign="top">Great capture! There is one very similar in this weeks Amateur Photographer (29th July). It finished 4th in the Shadows comp. At first glance I thought it was yours but I think yours is better. Congrats on your ribbon! <br/> <br/>Mike<br/></td>', 'Great capture! There is one very similar in this weeks Amateur Photographer (29th July). It finished 4th in the Shadows comp. At first glance I thought it was yours but I think yours is better. Congrats on your ribbon!  Mike', '2006-07-29 09:13:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(2674180, 364579, 30214, '<td valign="top">Great shot, Tim! Reminds me a refraction pattern on cover of "Dark side of the moon"...</td>', 'Great shot, Tim! Reminds me a refraction pattern on cover of "Dark side of the moon"...', '2006-07-29 15:27:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(2675093, 364108, 7969, '<td valign="top">Very very cool shot, nicely done!</td>', 'Very very cool shot, nicely done!', '2006-07-29 23:45:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(2676178, 363522, 37858, '<td valign="top">Trading Post Comment<br/> <br/>Great album.  I like everything about this picture except the rainbow stripe.  While lines is the theme, I think the unity of lines in the album was enough to carry this shot...it almost looks like you were unsure people would accept the lines in the album and on the label so you added a rainbow to satisfy the DNMC crowd.  Without the rainbow you get simplicity and harmonious color tones.  IMHO this photo is about the album; the rainbow competes for attention.  Other than that, I think this is a terrific shot...and I would have scored this higher than most people did.</td>', 'Trading Post Comment Great album.  I like everything about this picture except the rainbow stripe.  While lines is the theme, I think the unity of lines in the album was enough to carry this shot...it almost looks like you were unsure people would accept the lines in the album and on the label so you added a rainbow to satisfy the DNMC crowd.  Without the rainbow you get simplicity and harmonious color tones.  IMHO this photo is about the album; the rainbow competes for attention.  Other than that, I think this is a terrific shot...and I would have scored this higher than most people did.', '2006-07-30 14:42:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(2676209, 364717, 37858, '<td valign="top">My first reaction when viewing this photo is that it should place high in this challenge. My second thought was that there was so much going on in this shot that DPC voters might not appreciate it.  I am glad to see that my first thought was accurate.<br/> <br/>I love the colors and the floor boards most.  I also think the rustic subject matter adds much charm.  The whole photo is excellent, the way various lines work together.  The lighting is also perfect.<br/></td>', 'My first reaction when viewing this photo is that it should place high in this challenge. My second thought was that there was so much going on in this shot that DPC voters might not appreciate it.  I am glad to see that my first thought was accurate. I love the colors and the floor boards most.  I also think the rustic subject matter adds much charm.  The whole photo is excellent, the way various lines work together.  The lighting is also perfect.', '2006-07-30 15:07:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(2676251, 365611, 37858, '<td valign="top">Trading post Comment<br/> <br/>I like the green portion of the leaf and the many small veins.  Unfortunately, the brilliance of the main vein is overpowering.  It''s too blinding IMHO and works against the rest of the image.  I also wonder if you could have toned down the noise in the green area.  You don''t indicate what post processing you performed, but I think running the image through the NeatImage plug-in would have taken care of that.  There is potential here...but the focus should be on the green, not the white, portions of the photo.</td>', 'Trading post Comment I like the green portion of the leaf and the many small veins.  Unfortunately, the brilliance of the main vein is overpowering.  It''s too blinding IMHO and works against the rest of the image.  I also wonder if you could have toned down the noise in the green area.  You don''t indicate what post processing you performed, but I think running the image through the NeatImage plug-in would have taken care of that.  There is potential here...but the focus should be on the green, not the white, portions of the photo.', '2006-07-30 15:29:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(2676685, 366143, 32872, '<td valign="top">Thank you all for your constructive comments.  It really does help me.<br/> <br/>:)<br/> <br/></td>', 'Thank you all for your constructive comments.  It really does help me. :) ', '2006-07-30 19:11:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(2676783, 365525, 22734, '<td valign="top">Wow!!! Congratulations on your well earned BLUE.</td>', 'Wow!!! Congratulations on your well earned BLUE.', '2006-07-30 19:52:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(2676784, 364108, 22734, '<td valign="top">Great linear beauty here expertly captured and very well presented to win the day. Congratulations on your RED!</td>', 'Great linear beauty here expertly captured and very well presented to win the day. Congratulations on your RED!', '2006-07-30 19:53:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(2676789, 364931, 22734, '<td valign="top">Trip the light fantastic! Awesome in scope and color movement. Congratulations on your Yellow!</td>', 'Trip the light fantastic! Awesome in scope and color movement. Congratulations on your Yellow!', '2006-07-30 19:54:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(2676815, 363572, 52731, '<td valign="top">It''s surprising to me that this photograph only recieved one comment for this challenge. While the focus is a bit soft, the composition and set up are pretty decent. I like the vibrancy and rich tones of the green and think they work well with the warm tones of the wood. To make this have a higher score, a bit more sharpening should do the trick.<br/> <br/>Keep shooting!<br/> <br/>-Monica</td>', 'It''s surprising to me that this photograph only recieved one comment for this challenge. While the focus is a bit soft, the composition and set up are pretty decent. I like the vibrancy and rich tones of the green and think they work well with the warm tones of the wood. To make this have a higher score, a bit more sharpening should do the trick. Keep shooting! -Monica', '2006-07-30 20:06:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(2676917, 366082, 22734, '<td valign="top">Both deamatic and funny and inviting the viewer to egg along. Congratulations on your 4th placing. Nice work.</td>', 'Both deamatic and funny and inviting the viewer to egg along. Congratulations on your 4th placing. Nice work.', '2006-07-30 21:05:34.000000', NULL, 0),
