(3067849, 364772, 2490, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by yanko:</b></div><hr/><i> Shouldn''t the reason for this DQ be major element added? The use of USM is not spot editing. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>"Major Elements" <strike>is</strike> <b>was</b> not applicable to basic editing.  I still don''t understand the reason for DQ if USM actually created the effect.  Since Basic Editing as of the date of this challenge was "tool based" and USM was legal if applied to the entire image, I don''t understand the "spot editing" comment.  Was there additional editing that was truly spot editing, or was the miscommunicated USM usage actually all that was wrong?  Regardless of whether the DQ stands, was the image actually illegal????</td>', 'Originally posted by yanko: Shouldn''t the reason for this DQ be major element added? The use of USM is not spot editing.   "Major Elements" is was not applicable to basic editing.  I still don''t understand the reason for DQ if USM actually created the effect.  Since Basic Editing as of the date of this challenge was "tool based" and USM was legal if applied to the entire image, I don''t understand the "spot editing" comment.  Was there additional editing that was truly spot editing, or was the miscommunicated USM usage actually all that was wrong?  Regardless of whether the DQ stands, was the image actually illegal????', '2006-11-28 08:37:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(3095035, 363430, 17148, '<td valign="top">Im sorry that I just saw this but this shot is incredible. Mainly for the time spent preparing and the artistic value. Amazing jobshould have placed a bit higher also.</td>', 'Im sorry that I just saw this but this shot is incredible. Mainly for the time spent preparing and the artistic value. Amazing jobshould have placed a bit higher also.', '2006-12-07 00:30:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(3136932, 363430, 5112, '<td valign="top">Amanda, I missed this one before!  This is excellent work.  Love it.</td>', 'Amanda, I missed this one before!  This is excellent work.  Love it.', '2006-12-20 18:26:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(3157149, 363886, 25166, '<td valign="top">First time that I''ve taken a good look through your portfolio, and you''ve some stuff to be very proud of. I love this image. Clearly wasn''t to everybody''s liking during the challenge, but I really like it. The contrast is very strong and the position of the iris is bang on. Well crafted. Will keep an eye on your future submissions.</td>', 'First time that I''ve taken a good look through your portfolio, and you''ve some stuff to be very proud of. I love this image. Clearly wasn''t to everybody''s liking during the challenge, but I really like it. The contrast is very strong and the position of the iris is bang on. Well crafted. Will keep an eye on your future submissions.', '2006-12-28 18:41:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(3158123, 363886, 69008, '<td valign="top">This image really has an aborigonal flavor to it. The black area on the forehead makes the shape of the face in the image grab your attention, even in the thumbnails. It seems somewhere between body paint and dreamland rock drawings. The one sided composition is also a powerful part of what makes it work, as though she is peering out of a door frame into the room with you. The only distraction is the touch of light in the upper right corner, but maybe you left it to show the hair line there. I enjoy seeing what you have been doing as you have such a unique way of seeing and capturing what you see. <br/>Very creative and great imaging with the B&amp;W and high contrast. I can''t understand why it placed so low in the challenge.</td>', 'This image really has an aborigonal flavor to it. The black area on the forehead makes the shape of the face in the image grab your attention, even in the thumbnails. It seems somewhere between body paint and dreamland rock drawings. The one sided composition is also a powerful part of what makes it work, as though she is peering out of a door frame into the room with you. The only distraction is the touch of light in the upper right corner, but maybe you left it to show the hair line there. I enjoy seeing what you have been doing as you have such a unique way of seeing and capturing what you see. Very creative and great imaging with the B&W and high contrast. I can''t understand why it placed so low in the challenge.', '2006-12-29 00:44:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(3210271, 363430, 36628, '<td valign="top">Damn thats cool, well done</td>', 'Damn thats cool, well done', '2007-01-11 00:34:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(3213947, 366125, 48228, '<td valign="top">Gee, I saw this in the challenge and forgot to add it to my favorites, so correcting that right now. <br/>This is just awesome, and great colors, textures, and wonderful leading lines at natures best.</td>', 'Gee, I saw this in the challenge and forgot to add it to my favorites, so correcting that right now. This is just awesome, and great colors, textures, and wonderful leading lines at natures best.', '2007-01-11 18:02:56.000000', NULL, 0),
